            <ArticleTitle>Primary cutaneous histoplasmosis: a new presentation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>152-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A fifty-one year old man on chronic steroid therapy presented with a cellulitis-erysipelas-like eruption which proved to be histoplasmosis without demonstrable systemic involvement. This presentation deviates from the five previously reported cases, two nodular and three noduloulcerative, all of which presented as a self-limited, minimally tender lesion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
